<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="FB_MachineModeFromEPICS" Id="{e77c5ce7-1295-45e2-913d-511a3f59fc41}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
FB_MachineModeFromEPICS

Reads the machine-mode PV from the accelerator and publishes it in
ST_BeamParams.nMachineMode (BP.nMachineMode), raising a fast fault when the
readback is unusable.

The machine-mode values are declared once in PMPS_PARAM, so every PMPS component
that consumes nMachineMode (this block, FB_BeamClassFromEPICS,
FB_BeamClassWatcher, F_SafeBPCompare, F_SafeBPCompare0Rate) shares one
definition:

    PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_NC            = 0  NC (normal conducting, copper linac)
    PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_SC            = 1  SC (superconducting linac)
    PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_MISCONFIGURED = 2  Misconfigured (something in the link node not set correctly)
    PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_FAILSAFE      = 3  Fail-safe value written when the readback is unusable

NC and SC are the only modes usable for beam: the Misconfigured value is the
first unusable mode, so a readback at or above it raises the fast fault. When
the readback itself is not valid, BP.nMachineMode carries MACHINE_MODE_FAILSAFE,
the fast fault is raised and BP.xValid is cleared.

History:
2026-11-27  Machine-mode values moved to PMPS_PARAM constants (audit finding 1144).
*)
FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_MachineModeFromEPICS
VAR_IN_OUT
    BP : ST_BeamParams;
    fbMPS_MachineMode : FB_LREALFromEPICS;
    FFO : FB_HardwareFFOutput;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
    xError : BOOL;
END_VAR
VAR

    ffModeReadBack : FB_FastFault := (
        i_DevName := 'Arbiter',
        i_Desc := 'Issue with Machine mode readback from Accelerator. Gateway or EPICS connection. Must be fixed.',
        i_TypeCode := 16#313,
        i_xAutoReset:=True);
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[fbMPS_MachineMode();

IF fbMPS_MachineMode.bValid THEN
    BP.nMachineMode := LREAL_TO_USINT(fbMPS_MachineMode.fValue);
ELSE
    BP.nMachineMode := PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_FAILSAFE;
END_IF

// NC and SC are usable for beam; from the Misconfigured value upward the readback is rejected.
ffModeReadBack(i_xOK:=(fbMPS_MachineMode.bValid) AND fbMPS_MachineMode.fValue < USINT_TO_LREAL(PMPS_PARAM.MACHINE_MODE_MISCONFIGURED) , io_fbFFHWO:=FFO);

BP.xValid R= NOT fbMPS_MachineMode.bValid;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>